      "writtenOn": "2024-10-08T13:38:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking this is like the other `MatchWidth` in that it matches the width of the vector to determine the return type. I think this is a pretty common use-case, as we have builder functions that take vectors of indices (Swizzle, Access, etc).\n\nIf I make it take a length, then I guess we should rename it to something else. Maybe `VectorOrScaler(Type*, size_t len)` ?",
      "parentUuid": "256454cc_93da3975",
      "revId": "b539032672d2d0c4bd6d125cb851867c2c6a931f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
